All green. The fix is complete:

## What was wrong

In `format_risk_report (src/commands_risk_report.rs`), the row format string always appended `{CYAN}{signals_str}{RESET}` even when signals_str was empty. That emitted invisible ANSI color escape sequences after the path, so the new test `test_file_signal_tags_no_signals_no_tags` — which asserts the text after the path is pure whitespace when no signals fired — failed on the stray escape bytes.

## The fix

Wrapped the tag list in color codes only when it's non-empty:

```rust
let colored_signals = if signals_str.is_empty() {
    String::new()
} else {
    format!("{CYAN}{signals_str}{RESET}")
};
out.push_str(&format!(
    "  {YELLOW}{:.2}{RESET}   {td_display}  {padded_path}{colored_signals}\n",
    risk.score
));
```

No-signal rows now end in plain whitespace after the path (no hallucinated tags, no stray escapes), while signal-bearing rows still render `[churn, mut 50%]` in cyan.

